# Drafted by Gemini (R13 windmill), edited.

~ jonah_rescued
set jonah_saved
quest the_burning_mill rescued
Narrator: Soot streaks Jonah's cheeks, and the hot draft off the burning timbers smells of parched grain and singed wool.
jonah_sawyer [afraid]: Thought that beam was gonna give before you climbed up here. Everything went mad so fast, I do not even know what I am looking at anymore.
* What did you and Martha quarrel over? -> jonah_quarrel
* Tell us what happened to Liza. -> jonah_liza
* We should get out of here now. -> jonah_out

~ jonah_quarrel
set secret_jonah
jonah_sawyer [sad]: It was the silver in her cellar chest, the coin set aside for the church bell. I took it when our winter stores ran thin.
jonah_sawyer [weary]: When Martha found the lock forced, I told her old Isaac's ghost must have walked and hid it. I started this whole bitter mess with a lie.
-> jonah_rescued

~ jonah_liza
jonah_sawyer [afraid]: She came up the ladder wearing that carved pumpkin for a head, reaching out like she knew me. I swung the iron bar before I saw her apron.
jonah_sawyer [sad]: Crushed her straw hand right against the post, and she cried out in Liza's own voice. God help me, that thing has my sister inside it.
-> jonah_rescued

~ jonah_out
if not quest.fields_of_the_crow >= investigating
quest fields_of_the_crow investigating
endif
jonah_sawyer [weary]: Aye, the roof timbers will not hold much longer. Lead on down the stairs and I will keep right behind you.
-> END

~ liza_plea
set liza_asked
Narrator: Dry corn husks rustle inside her linen sleeves, and a faint breath of sweet squash rises from her carved grin.
liza_sawyer [afraid]: Please keep the lanterns back from my hem, if you have any mercy. If the fire takes this straw, there is nothing left of me to wake.
-> END

